:"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:09:24-07:00","id":140261,"title":"","content":"While they're great sheets. And really you go above and beyond anything I've ever seen, or what most of us deserve. After printing one out. I still can't get over the black background over the attributes. I also think that &quot;Cipher&quot; and &quot;Final Truth&quot; should be in black. But this is more of a personal preference. It's not like I'm not using the sheets as is. I just don't find the Attributes using an inverted color scheme and then everything out standard with a washed out background makes for a friendly page.<br /> Gee I read that and I sound like a horrible person. I'm considering handing out colored pencils during character creation so everyone can color in the attributes and still see the point totals. I know, I know there are at max five and my players can count backwards but one is new to WOD and the other to roleplaying so I'm looking at it from an inexperienced point of view. Or maybe I'm biased and use to the Mage sheet since I've been running that forever. I dunno' their still awesome though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T08:29:07-07:00","id":140564,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm...let me think on it and I'll see if I can come up with a better solution for you.<br /> <br /> Is the page background ok? Are the regular section dividers ok? If so, then I'll see 